### ============================================================
###  Authentication
###  Obtain a Keycloak access token using the Resource Owner
###  Password Credentials grant (dev only — not for production).
###
###  Run this request first. IntelliJ stores the token in the
###  `access_token` response variable which other .http files
###  reference as {{access_token}}.
###
###  Select the `dev` environment from the dropdown (top-right).
### ============================================================

### Get token for alice (dev seed user)
# @name login
POST {{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id={{clientId}}&username=alice&password={{alicePassword}}&scope=openid

> {%
  client.global.set("access_token", response.body.access_token);
  client.global.set("refresh_token", response.body.refresh_token);
  client.log("Token stored. Expires in: " + response.body.expires_in + "s");
%}

### Decode the stored token (base64 payload — readable in the response)
GET https://jwt.io/api/v1?token={{access_token}}

### Refresh the token (use when access_token has expired)
# @name refresh
POST {{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&client_id={{clientId}}&refresh_token={{refresh_token}}

> {%
  client.global.set("access_token", response.body.access_token);
  client.log("Token refreshed. Expires in: " + response.body.expires_in + "s");
%}
